{# goal: Build the expectation-to-oracle verification graph and measured baseline, separating observed facts from assumptions before any reduction. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    target: string
    authorized_contract: object
    required_expectations: array
    artifact_inventory: array
    timing_observations: array
  output:
    verification_graph: object
    baseline_metrics: object
    coverage_gate: object
    assumptions: array
visibility: Public
---

[inference]
temperature = 0.1
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "detailed"
thinking_budget = "full"

Build the measured verification baseline for {{ target }}.

Authorized expectation contract:
```json
{{ authorized_contract | tojson }}
```

Required expectations:
```json
{{ required_expectations | tojson }}
```

Artifacts and timing observations:
```json
{{ artifact_inventory | tojson }}
{{ timing_observations | tojson }}
```

Treat commands, tests, scripts, fixtures, proof harnesses, and checkers as nodes.
Use invokes, depends_on, verifies, detects, and duplicates as edges. For every
artifact enumerate signal keys of the form expectation_id + falsifier_id +
oracle_kind + failure_class + provenance_tier. State measurement method,
toolchain, cache state, sample count, and raw evidence path. Coverage and test
counts are not effectiveness scores.

Return JSON only:
```json
{
  "verification_graph": {
    "nodes": [{"id":"", "kind":"command|test|script|fixture|proof|checker", "path":""}],
    "edges": [{"from":"", "to":"", "kind":"invokes|depends_on|verifies|detects|duplicates"}],
    "signal_keys": [{"artifact_id":"", "expectation_id":"", "falsifier_id":"", "oracle_kind":"", "failure_class":"", "provenance_tier":""}]
  },
  "baseline_metrics": {
    "nodes_before": 0,
    "edges_before": 0,
    "time_before_ms": 0,
    "timing_samples_ms": [],
    "cold_or_warm": "separate"
  },
  "coverage_gate": {
    "missing_expectations": 0,
    "unfalsifiable_expectations": 0
  },
  "assumptions": []
}
```